<<~ ahu slot=`#/invitation`>>
! Example Five ~ two materials, no compulsory concept board

This short Folio uses the same eight-dimension nucleus but adds only the independent material scopes and comparison that the work earns.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/folio-sigils`>>
```tiddlywiki
<<art worktype=`physical two-panel textile and painted-wood diptych` subject=`continuity interrupted by an uneven seam` read=`contact without complete merger` imagery=`one stretched cloth panel with thick stitched curves; one quiet wood panel with a pale rubbed arc` treatment=`visible knots and raw cloth contrasting matte pigment rubbed into wood grain` composition=`unequal adjacent panels separated by a narrow dark interval` relation=`the curved mark appears to continue across the seam, but the two materials interrupt its rhythm` depiction-scope=`the diptych itself; no studio, artist, or spectator depicted`>>
<<art-counterpoint first=`stitched curved line on cloth` second=`rubbed pigment arc on wood` tension=`continuity of gesture meets refusal of material continuity` evidence=`two misaligned arc ends approach the same dark seam`>>
<<art-facture scope=`left panel` support=`coarse undyed woven cloth` medium=`waxed thread` handling=`visible needle spacing, loose knots and slight puckering`>>
<<art-facture scope=`right panel` support=`unfinished timber` medium=`thin matte earth pigment` handling=`pigment follows open grain and leaves pale voids`>>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/critical-reading`>>
The diptych need not show preliminary studies, labels, pinned references or a photographic montage. A digital picture may simulate these materials; visual facture alone does not prove a physical diptych was manufactured. Only the artist's actual production record can support that claim.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/noninheritance`>>
Neither textile nor two-panel presentation is a procedural default. `art-counterpoint` is warranted by one visible shared gesture, not merely by two nearby objects.
<<~/ahu>>

